---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
import Email from '../components/Email.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Courtney Root, a cybersecurity engineer with 8+ years in the field, focused on AI and cloud security.">
  <div class="about-intro">
    <img src="/headshot.webp" alt="Courtney Root" width="220" height="275" class="headshot" />
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Hi, I'm Courtney.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I've worked in cybersecurity for more than eight years, including the last four securing cloud products
        used by customers at scale. These days I spend most of my time thinking about what AI changes for attackers,
        defenders, and the people who have to decide where to invest.
      </p>
      <p>
        I hold a Master of Cybersecurity from Georgia Tech, where I studied everything from incident response
        to cyber deterrence policy. Now I'm finishing an MBA at UC Berkeley's Haas School of Business (Class of 2027),
        which is where the "security as a business decision" thread in my writing comes from.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm a big believer in capture-the-flag events as an on-ramp into the field. Outside of work, I spend a lot of
        my time volunteering, which you can read about <a href="#volunteering">below</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What I believe about AI and security</h2>
    <div class="thesis thesis-about">
      <p class="thesis-lead">
        AI agents turn every input into a potential instruction, so security has to shift from protecting data
        to governing what software is allowed to do.
      </p>
      <p class="thesis-follow">
        That only works when business, engineering and security set those limits together, so customers stay
        protected and teams keep moving fast.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p>Everything I write comes back to that idea. <a href="/writing/">Read the writing</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="volunteering">Volunteering</h2>
    <p>Giving back is a big part of my life. Here's where I spend that time.</p>

    <div class="volunteer">
      <div class="volunteer-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.sfmfoodbank.org/">SF-Marin Food Bank</a></h3>
        <p class="volunteer-when">Every month</p>
        <p>
          I pack boxes for the food bank's home delivery program for seniors, and sort and pack food for people who
          need it. The food bank's mission is to end hunger in San Francisco and Marin counties, and it supplies
          groceries to about 15,000 households every week.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="volunteer-item">
        <h3>Bay Area parks and open spaces</h3>
        <p class="volunteer-when">Every other month</p>
        <p>
          I join restoration projects at different parks and open spaces around the Bay Area, helping care for the
          places that make living here special.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="volunteer-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.wicys.org/">Women in Cybersecurity (WiCyS)</a></h3>
        <p class="volunteer-when">2027 Program Committee</p>
        <p>
          I review talk and workshop proposals for the WiCyS 2027 conference, helping choose sessions that are
          practical, fresh and useful for people at every stage of their security careers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="volunteer-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.playworks.org/">Playworks</a></h3>
        <p class="volunteer-when">National board project, through mid-2027</p>
        <p>
          Playworks helps schools and youth programs create recess and play where every child can join in. I'm working
          with its national board over eight months to survey board members, analyze the results, and define
          improvements to how the board engages.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="bios">Bios for organizers</h2>
    <p>Copy whichever fits your program.</p>
    <h3>Short</h3>
    <div class="bio-card">
      <p>
        Courtney Root is a cybersecurity engineer with more than eight years in the field, focused on AI and cloud
        security, and an MBA candidate at UC Berkeley Haas.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h3>Long</h3>
    <div class="bio-card">
      <p>
        Courtney Root is a cybersecurity engineer with more than eight years in the field, including four years
        securing cloud products for customers. Courtney's work and writing focus on securing AI systems, using AI to
        strengthen defense, and helping business leaders make good security decisions. Courtney holds a Master of
        Cybersecurity from Georgia Tech, is completing an MBA at UC Berkeley's Haas School of Business (Class of 2027),
        and serves on the WiCyS 2027 Program Committee.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p><a href="/og-image.jpg">Download a high-resolution headshot</a></p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Email <Email />, or find me on <a href={SITE.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a> and <a href={SITE.links.github}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
